{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Balaam said, etc. — I have sinned, for I did not, etc.</b> His saying <b>I have sinned</b> corresponds to what they alluded to in the statement ״יָרַט הַדֶּרֶךְ״ etc., and corresponding to His saying ״לָמָּה הִכִּיתָ״ etc. he said ״כִּי לֹא יָדַעְתִּי״ etc. And his saying <b>and now</b> [means]: do teshuvah for what he intended to do, and corresponding to the journey he said ״אִם רַע בְּעֵינֶיךָ אָשׁוּבָה״. And he said ״לִי״ — a spark of prophecy flashed in him, that he has a good advantage in turning back."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:46.482028405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}